        "sys_immortal_killer_move"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At San Cha mountain inheritance grounds, Long Qing Tian is named a famous poison path Gu Master who kills three Shang clan elders with poison and lifts demonic path morale until Wu clan’s Elder Wu Tong Shen holds him back.",
      "chapters": [
        326
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-the-path-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_san_cha_mountain",
        "char_long_qing_tian",
        "sys_gu_master",
        "fac_shang_clan",
        "fac_wu_clan",
        "char_wu_tong_shen"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Lang Ya land spirit identifies Immortal Gu Woman’s Heart as a poison path Immortal Gu with a lethal poison. Feeding it requires the hearts of women, and that feeding is also the process of continually refining and promoting the Gu, so more hearts make a more powerful poison. Female variant human hearts can substitute at a worse effect.",
      "chapters": [
        663
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "womans-heart-immortal-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_lang_ya_land_spirit",
        "gu_womans_heart"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Against He Feng Yang’s crane groups, one mysterious Gu Immortal uses the poison path killer move Killer Bee Stab, raining needles whose poison kills flying cranes on contact and disintegrates their flesh. He Feng Yang identifies that fighter as a poison path Gu Immortal, paired with a wind path Gu Immortal partner.",
      "chapters": [
        703
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
